{
  "title": "Lo zaino, i libri e l'amica",
  "translation": "The backpack, the books and the friend",
  "topics": "Gender and number of nouns, definite and indefinite articles",
  "grammar": {
    "explain": [
      "Every Italian noun is masculine or feminine. Usually the ending tells you which. Words in *-e* can be either, so learn them with their article.",
      {
        "table": {
          "head": [
            "",
            "Singular",
            "Plural"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Masculine in -o",
              "ragazz**o**",
              "ragazz**i**"
            ],
            [
              "Feminine in -a",
              "ragazz**a**",
              "ragazz**e**"
            ],
            [
              "Masculine or feminine in -e",
              "il can**e**, la chiav**e**",
              "i can**i**, le chiav**i**"
            ]
          ]
        }
      },
      "Words ending in an accented vowel, like *città* and *caffè*, do not change in the plural: *la città, le città*.",
      "The article depends on the gender, the number and the first letter of the next word.",
      {
        "table": {
          "head": [
            "Next word begins with",
            "the (singular)",
            "the (plural)",
            "a / an"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Masculine: a consonant",
              "**il** libro",
              "**i** libri",
              "**un** libro"
            ],
            [
              "Masculine: s + consonant, z, ps, gn",
              "**lo** zaino",
              "**gli** zaini",
              "**uno** zaino"
            ],
            [
              "Masculine: a vowel",
              "**l'**amico",
              "**gli** amici",
              "**un** amico"
            ],
            [
              "Feminine: a consonant",
              "**la** casa",
              "**le** case",
              "**una** casa"
            ],
            [
              "Feminine: a vowel",
              "**l'**amica",
              "**le** amiche",
              "**un'**amica"
            ]
          ]
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  "use": {
